No idea about that particular case, but a lot of beginning players
probably don't know about #enhance.  I don't think I found about it
until I started reading spoilers.  None of the messages in the game
itself suggest it, and nethack is so full of obscure extended commands
(e.g. #sit) that it's easy to miss.  Especially when the command name
gives no indication of what it actually does.

It Would Be Nice If the "you feel more confident" message would
actually go on to say: "Try the #enhance command to advance your
skills."  I know some might consider that to be breaking the fourth
wall or whatever, but I'd say in this case it'd be justified.

